    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:c3205ac1e20a266d",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "3f5dccbd06f838f337625e60122ebdafc6e5568922c130716854e78e5e79cf45",
      "text": "Today you will visit Iguazu Falls, a system of 275 cascades on the border between Brazil and Argentina. The name Iguazu comes from the Guarani language and means “Big Water”.\n\nWalking trails and viewing platforms let you see the falls from different angles and approach the famous Devil’s Throat, where a powerful torrent plunges down and fine spray fills the air.",
